# `dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer`

Minimises a black box that fails at many points with Disco MADS, which looks for valid points around each failure.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer(const std::function<dfo::BlackboxEvaluation(const pluss::Series &)> &blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::DiscoMadsConfig &config = {});
template <class Fn> dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer(Fn &&blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::DiscoMadsConfig &config = {});
```

## What It Does

For a simulation that does not always converge. A failed or non-finite evaluation stays a failure for the search, as in plain MADS, but Disco also looks around each failure: up to `rescue_trials` nearby points (random offsets of radius `rescue_radius`, shrinking by `rescue_radius_decay` each trial) are evaluated and any valid result is kept as a candidate, so valid information near failures is not thrown away. At the end the best candidate replaces the search result if it is better. The rescue only starts once a share `rescue_failure_rate` of the evaluations has failed (after a warm-up of 20 calls), because plain MADS copes with an occasional failure on its own; the rescue calls are extra calls of the black box.

## Parameters

`Fn &&blackbox`
: A callable returning a `BlackboxEvaluation`, a `Series` of objectives or a number.

`const pluss::Series &initial`
: The starting point.

`const dfo::DiscoMadsConfig &config`
: The settings.

## Returns

A [`BlackboxAdvancedOutcome`](BlackboxAdvancedOutcome.md).

## Errors

- A black box that returns neither objectives nor a failure flag throws on the first call.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A black box in which 80% of the points fail (it returns NaN there). The minimum of `(x₀ − 2)² + (x₁ − 1)²` is 0. Plain MADS stalls at 4.99, Disco reaches a better point, with more calls.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <cmath>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto make_box = [](double rate, std::int64_t *calls) {
    return [rate, calls](const Series &x) {
      ++*calls;
      dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
      const double a = x.select(0, 0).item<double>(), b = x.select(0, 1).item<double>();
      double h = std::sin(12345.678 * a + 9876.543 * b + 0.5) * 43758.5453;   // a fixed pseudo-random fraction of points fails
      h -= std::floor(h);
      e.objectives = (h < rate) ? pluss::make_series(std::nan("")).reshape({1}) : (x - pluss::series::make({2.0, 1.0})).square().sum().reshape({1});
      return e;
    };
  };
  std::int64_t plain_calls = 0, disco_calls = 0;
  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig plain;
  plain.max_evaluations = 3000;
  dfo::DiscoMadsConfig disco;
  disco.base = plain;
  const Series start = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome a = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(make_box(0.8, &plain_calls), start, plain);
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome b = dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer(make_box(0.8, &disco_calls), start, disco);
  out.writeln("plain MADS: minimum =", a.scalarized_minimum, ", calls =", plain_calls);
  out.writeln("Disco     : minimum =", b.scalarized_minimum, ", calls =", disco_calls);
}
```

### Example 2

The number of rescue trials. More trials per failure find a better point and cost more calls.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <cmath>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto make_box = [](double rate, std::int64_t *calls) {
    return [rate, calls](const Series &x) {
      ++*calls;
      dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
      const double a = x.select(0, 0).item<double>(), b = x.select(0, 1).item<double>();
      double h = std::sin(12345.678 * a + 9876.543 * b + 0.5) * 43758.5453;   // a fixed pseudo-random fraction of points fails
      h -= std::floor(h);
      e.objectives = (h < rate) ? pluss::make_series(std::nan("")).reshape({1}) : (x - pluss::series::make({2.0, 1.0})).square().sum().reshape({1});
      return e;
    };
  };
  for (const std::int64_t trials : {3, 12}) {
    std::int64_t calls = 0;
    dfo::DiscoMadsConfig config;
    config.base.max_evaluations = 3000;
    config.rescue_trials = trials;
    const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer(make_box(0.8, &calls), pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), config);
    out.writeln("rescue trials", trials, ": minimum =", o.scalarized_minimum, ", calls =", calls);
  }
}
```

### Example 3

A mild failure rate. With 30% of the points failing, plain MADS copes: the rescue stays off below the default threshold of 50% and the two runs are identical.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <cmath>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto make_box = [](double rate, std::int64_t *calls) {
    return [rate, calls](const Series &x) {
      ++*calls;
      dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
      const double a = x.select(0, 0).item<double>(), b = x.select(0, 1).item<double>();
      double h = std::sin(12345.678 * a + 9876.543 * b + 0.5) * 43758.5453;   // a fixed pseudo-random fraction of points fails
      h -= std::floor(h);
      e.objectives = (h < rate) ? pluss::make_series(std::nan("")).reshape({1}) : (x - pluss::series::make({2.0, 1.0})).square().sum().reshape({1});
      return e;
    };
  };
  std::int64_t plain_calls = 0, disco_calls = 0;
  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig plain;
  plain.max_evaluations = 3000;
  dfo::DiscoMadsConfig disco;
  disco.base = plain;
  const Series start = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  out.writeln("plain MADS: minimum =", dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(make_box(0.3, &plain_calls), start, plain).scalarized_minimum, ", calls =", plain_calls);
  out.writeln("Disco     : minimum =", dfo::discomads_blackbox_minimizer(make_box(0.3, &disco_calls), start, disco).scalarized_minimum, ", calls =", disco_calls);
}
```

